1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the setting sun
drifting over the Nakagawa

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and
my shoes went flying too

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,920
onto the head of the carpenter
I was putting in a choke hold

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I'm still just a kid

5
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:44,220
even if I chase after some energy somewhere

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
dull and lackluster,
one yawn after another, nothing changes

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
the streetscape feels strangely gentle

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,180
from the pointed-hat purification fountain

9
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls into the vast sky

10
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too, it will end just like this

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,720
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness again, they say

12
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:24,680
Talking nonsense, I finally realized,
because I'm such a fool

13
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:31,500
A baseball tournament that calls the storm

14
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:43,100
Isn't this Yuki Aikawa! I'm a huge fan!

15
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:43,380
What is it?

16
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:45,340
What's this?

17
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:49,200
She's coming to the Kameari shopping
street for a charity concert in two weeks.

18
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,840
Lucky!

19
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:53,340
Let's get her autograph.

20
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:54,260
That's the senior officer's...

21
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,660
Look at this.

22
00:01:58,700 --> 00:01:59,420
What's what?

23
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:03,100
Is the Kameari Minami shopping
street holding a charity concert too?

24
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:04,020
Lucky!

25
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,440
We're also scheduled to come in two weeks.

26
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:09,360
What's going on?

27
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:10,840
Anyway,

28
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,440
due to a mix-up at the office,

29
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:14,460
it looks like we got double-booked.

30
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:18,960
The Kameari and Minami shopping streets don't get along,
do they?

31
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:21,180
I wonder what they plan to do.

32
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,480
They're going to settle it with a sandlot baseball game,
apparently.

33
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:24,780
Sandlot baseball?

34
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:30,580
Now that you mention it, the Kameari shopping
street people were practicing earlier.

35
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:44,720
I don't care who wins,
as long as I get to meet Yuki Aikawa.

36
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:49,660
No, no, no, no!

37
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:53,300
I got distracted by Yuki-chan
and forgot to book the game!

38
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,240
Hurry up!

39
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:07,180
Is the reservation still okay? Welcome!

40
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,260
...kilo

41
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:24,160
Is that really Kiyohara? How did he end up in a place like this?
Actually, he's the grandmother from the parents' home of the president's wife of the company my son's classmate's father does business with.

42
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:32,040
A distant relative of hers played against Kiyohara in Little League,
so he's helping out at the shop through that connection.

43
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:35,040
So now he's a member of the shopping street.

44
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:39,140
I'll do my best in the upcoming game too.

45
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,860
I see. With Kiyohara playing,
it's as good as a win.

46
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:45,360
I'll cheer for you too, Chairman.

47
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:47,440
Don't forget Yuki-chan's autograph!

48
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,540
Leave it to me.

49
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,360
Leave it to you, then.

50
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:01,080
What? Kiyohara?!

51
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,300
It's the same guy I saw on TV.

52
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:06,780
Mizuhara's such a dirty, underhanded guy.

53
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:09,620
Bringing pro players to
a sandlot baseball game!

54
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,800
What do we do, Ozaki-san?

55
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:14,000
Against pro players?

56
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,360
No amount of practice will let us win.

57
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:20,240
If they're bringing in ringers,
then we'll bring in ringers too.

58
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:23,600
We can't afford to lose this game.

59
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,040
But we don't have any ringers lined up.

60
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:33,680
Isn't there anyone who could help?

61
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:42,100
Hey! Give me back my lunch!

62
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:46,080
Hey, hand it over!

63
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:57,140
Wait!

64
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,120
What brute strength!

65
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:11,180
Superhuman stamina and
cockroach-like vitality!

66
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:14,360
In our town, the only one who
can match Kiyohara is that guy,

67
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,840
Kankichi Ryotsu.

68
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:19,540
Just go home already, go home.

69
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,780
How ridiculous.

70
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:27,500
A sandlot ringer won't
even last one inning anyway!

71
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:31,360
If we win,
you'll get to see Yuki Aikawa up close!

72
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:34,720
Even if we lose, you can still see her.

73
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:38,120
Figures he wouldn't agree so easily.

74
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,740
Then we have no choice.
Let's use our last-resort trick.

75
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:50,760
That's the total amount of debt
owed to our shopping street.

76
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:53,160
Let's get it back right away.

77
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,320
W-what a dirty trick!

78
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:56,540
You said you'd wait until the bonus!

79
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:00,000
So, how did it go?

80
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:01,820
Pay it back right now!

81
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:28,420
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

82
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,360
At least 20 percent.

83
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,180
No way.

84
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:32,940
Then 50 percent.

85
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:33,900
No way.

86
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:34,980
Then 80 percent.

87
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:36,520
No, no, no way!

88
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:39,240
Then just cancel it all.

89
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:41,700
Alright, I'll make a deal with you.

90
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:46,280
I understand how much you all care
about rebuilding the shopping street.

91
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:51,220
Though I'm not much use, let me lend
a hand for the Kameari shopping street.

92
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:53,500
So the debts are cancelled, right?

93
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:08,220
Why do I have to play too?

94
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:12,480
Because the shopping street guys are
worried about their physical strength.

95
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:15,920
But I've never played baseball before.

96
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:22,500
Now, the game between Kameari shopping street
and Kameari Minami shopping street will begin.

97
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:28,660
Top of the first inning,
Kameari Minami shopping street batting.

98
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:33,240
Batter number one,
Sarashina Soba Demaimoshi, Carl Lewis.

99
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:41,180
Come on!

100
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,180
Nice!

101
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:47,040
The superstar of the track and field world,
Carl Lewis.

102
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:49,200
So it wasn't just Kiyohara?

103
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:55,740
The cousin of my daughter's
friend's acquaintance

104
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:59,780
is someone we got to know
through the internet, Carl.

105
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:05,980
Even if he's the world's best
at the 100 meters and long jump,

106
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:07,800
baseball is for amateurs

107
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:10,360
should be, right?

108
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:17,060
Good, we got him out!

109
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:18,560
That's strange!

110
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:30,180
Second base,
beauty salon apprentice Kimiko Date.

111
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:33,700
Now it's a women's tennis player!

112
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:37,820
I wonder if she's also an
acquaintance of Ms. Mizuhara?

113
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:39,220
I don't know about that.

114
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:42,040
The tennis player

115
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:45,500
can really hit

116
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:55,680
Go for it!

117
00:08:55,680 --> 00:09:00,380
This time for sure!

118
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:05,740
Batting third: opposing side's shop part-timer,
Hana Takano

119
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:07,000
Hana Takano, do your best!

120
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,360
What, you're still here?

121
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,140
Senpai, look!

122
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:32,080
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

123
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:37,560
Aren't you the one breaking the rules,
using ringers who aren't even store employees?

124
00:09:37,560 --> 00:09:39,620
Stop making excuses.

125
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:42,980
If that's how you want it,

126
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:53,360
if we hit them with pitches
and get everyone ejected,

127
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:56,860
we win by default.

128
00:09:56,860 --> 00:10:20,720
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

129
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:25,580
Pitches like that won't work on pros.

130
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:37,140
Damn it, if it's come to this -

131
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:39,500
Got it!

132
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:55,820
I've never had this many
taken by just one person.

133
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:59,160
The difference in strength is too great.
You should stop.

134
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:02,020
Don't be stupid, my debts are on the line!

135
00:11:02,020 --> 00:11:04,080
I'm not giving up over something like this!

136
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:07,960
But senpai, please look at that.

137
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:18,060
That's Momo from the major leagues!

138
00:11:18,060 --> 00:11:19,820
Nooo!

139
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,860
Honda! Get on base even if you have to die!

140
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:24,660
No way...

141
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:27,680
Gray ball!

142
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:35,960
Strike!

143
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:38,720
Hey! Mix in a breaking ball,
not just fastballs!

144
00:11:39,580 --> 00:11:41,260
Strike!

145
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:43,700
Strike!

146
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:44,560
Batter's out!

147
00:11:48,820 --> 00:11:49,420
Sorry.

148
00:11:49,420 --> 00:11:50,440
Listen,

149
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:54,020
Hey, hey,
at this rate there won't be a game, Nomo.

150
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,020
Go easy on them a little.

151
00:11:56,740 --> 00:11:57,180
Yes.

152
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,120
Bring it.

153
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:05,440
With this, I can hit it.

154
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,220
A single to right field!

155
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:10,780
Maezono!

156
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:15,760
Out!

157
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:20,720
Dammit, if it's come to this,
I'll do it myself!

158
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:24,860
Yes!

159
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:33,280
Was that the pole vaulter Bubu?

160
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,200
This is hopeless!

161
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,160
Out!

162
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,380
Three outs, change!

163
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:47,000
Nice!

164
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:16,700
Whoa!

165
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:25,380
Yay!

166
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:47,660
Rain?

167
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:54,420
What do you say? It's starting to rain,
so let's call it a day here.

168
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:57,500
What? What's going to happen to the game?

169
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:02,780
Of course we're winning.
We've got a 23-run lead!

170
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,840
Or do you mean they can
still make a comeback?

171
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:11,320
Let's just give up already.

172
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:12,900
Yeah, exactly.

173
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:15,660
We can always arrange for
Yuki to come another time.

174
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:17,240
No, that won't do.

175
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:20,840
At this rate,
our dream of zero debt will vanish.

176
00:14:21,740 --> 00:14:23,940
Then let's call the game here.

177
00:14:24,380 --> 00:14:25,020
Wait!

178
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:27,380
The game is only halfway over!

179
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:30,880
We've only just started to get going.

180
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:33,400
Ryo-san, I understand how you feel, but...

181
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:34,700
You guys...

182
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:38,420
You said we absolutely couldn't lose today's game,
didn't you?

183
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:42,160
Was your resolve really that flimsy?

184
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,500
And you pro players on that side,

185
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:50,320
if you're going to run away
from this little bit of rain,

186
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:52,280
you can hardly call
yourselves true sportsmen.

187
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:56,120
Pros are supposed to fight through any conditions,
aren't they?

188
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:58,220
What are you talking about?

189
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:00,080
Think about the situation.

190
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:02,060
It's fine, Mizuhara-san.

191
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:05,380
We have our pride as professionals too.

192
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:07,280
Understood.

193
00:15:08,420 --> 00:15:08,980
Let's keep playing until now.

194
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:12,400
No matter what happens,
don't call off the game.

195
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:17,420
But even if we keep going,

196
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:19,880
No, it's the senior's way.

197
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:22,620
Maybe they have some kind of strategy.

198
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:28,360
If the conditions get worse,
it'll be our advantage.

199
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:43,880
No holding back! Finish them off quickly!

200
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:46,480
Yes, understood.

201
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:53,040
But I can't see well.

202
00:15:58,560 --> 00:15:59,360
Damn it!

203
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,280
My hand slipped!

204
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:09,220
Aaaaaah!

205
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:14,320
That was deliberate, of course.

206
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:17,440
They're showing their true colors right away

207
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:19,780
I'm already...

208
00:16:21,340 --> 00:16:25,120
With this Skinny, spin, spin, spin!

209
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:27,440
Yes! We got one run back!

210
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:36,300
And we're not giving you another run either!

211
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,360
Doppelgänger Magic Ball

212
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,220
Strike

213
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:48,860
Batter out

214
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:50,040
That's dirty!

215
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:52,120
You threw mud at the same time, too.

216
00:16:52,940 --> 00:16:55,960
Do you have any proof you did it on purpose?

217
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,357
Kiyohara, I didn't mean any harm,

218
00:16:59,407 --> 00:17:03,060
but with this rain, mud just got on my hand.
Forgive me.

219
00:17:04,580 --> 00:17:07,180
Yeah, bad conditions affect us both equally.

220
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:09,580
Ball.

221
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:14,160
When it gets like this, the senior
player really comes alive, you know.

222
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:22,460
Damn it! What are they doing!

223
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:44,500
A heavy rain, thunder, and flood warning
has just been issued for the Tokyo area.

224
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:48,920
Residents near rivers in particular,
please take extra care.

225
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:51,180
The risk of disaster is also growing.

226
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:55,300
We received word from the ward's
emergency response headquarters.

227
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:59,280
Reiko Akimoto, advise the households
along the river to evacuate.

228
00:17:59,280 --> 00:17:59,860
Yes.

229
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:06,820
A heavy rain, strong wind, thunder, and
precipitation warning has just been issued.

230
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:11,500
Anyone living along the river,
please evacuate to the nearest shelter.

231
00:18:17,020 --> 00:18:18,840
The river water is overflowing.

232
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:22,940
Continuing the game
any longer is impossible.

233
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:24,340
Just end it.

234
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:26,880
If you're fine with losing,

235
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:28,280
we can end it right now.

236
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:30,800
Don't say such a stupid thing.

237
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:33,420
We're still the ones ahead, you know.

238
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:35,880
But the momentum of the game is on our side.

239
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:38,520
They've closed the gap to just three runs,
after all.

240
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:40,880
No matter what happens,

241
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:42,820
I told you we're not canceling the game.

242
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:45,040
We're going to keep playing!

243
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,920
Senpai,
Honda and the others are being swept away!

244
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:57,700
Never mind, we can still play baseball
even if one or two are missing.

245
00:18:58,520 --> 00:19:01,740
Hah, deadly skipping stone, Tōhō!

246
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:05,140
Everyone, please stay calm and evacuate.

247
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:08,340
Don't panic,
please stay calm and act carefully.

248
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:10,020
Everyone, please calm down.

249
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:11,980
This way, this way!

250
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:13,500
Everyone, calm down.

251
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:14,820
Please stay calm and evacuate.

252
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:15,520
Help!

253
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:17,700
Honda and...

254
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:18,920
being swept away!

255
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:38,980


256
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:40,180
Those people went crazy

257
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:41,640
Whoa!

258
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:43,620
Help!

259
00:19:49,620 --> 00:19:52,700
Take the gap and run!
No, it's a swimming home run!

260
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,040
Iwasaki-san, please!

261
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:54,660
Yes!

262
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:00,000
Iwasaki from the women's swim team!

263
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:02,280
Where?

264
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:05,320
There it is!

265
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:17,320
Yay!

266
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:18,120
Yay! We tied it!

267
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:19,520
Yō-chan!

268
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:24,140
It's dangerous there! Evacuate right away!

269
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:27,703
Don't be stupid!
We finally caught up to tie it!

270
00:20:27,753 --> 00:20:29,380
There's no way we're stopping now!

271
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:30,540
Whoa!

272
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:34,000
Help!

273
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:39,420
If the pitcher's gone, we'll win by default

274
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:40,920
I'm still here.

275
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:47,400
I have pitching experience
from my high school days.

276
00:20:48,460 --> 00:20:50,400
Just as I thought, Kiyohara showed up.

277
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:30,720


278
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:32,240
They're still bickering.

279
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:34,700
By the way, what happened to the game?

280
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:35,480
Well...

281
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:40,840
Ryo-chan

282
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:50,700
Here I go!

283
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:58,400
Good luck!

284
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:23,240
Yay! It's a walk-off!

285
00:22:35,620 --> 00:22:39,200
It's true! I really hit a walk-off home run!

286
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:43,000
Fine, fine, I'll take Ryo-san's word for it.

287
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:49,640
So that settles it. Aikawa Yuki-chan will
be coming to our Kameari shopping street.

288
00:22:50,600 --> 00:22:54,300
And again, there's no one who can
prove Ryo-san's home run, right?

289
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:58,920
The umpire's calls from the top
of the ninth were all washed away!

290
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:03,520
Are you saying you don't
believe a police officer?

291
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:07,380
You're the one who always says
not to believe what Ryo-san says!

292
00:23:09,540 --> 00:23:11,760
Hey, my debts are wiped out, right?

293
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:20,240
This is bad.
Because of yesterday's heavy rain...

294
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:23,040
I hear Yuki-chan can't
get back from her tour stop.

295
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:27,080
Then what about today's event?

296
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:31,140
Either way, it's called off.

297
00:23:31,140 --> 00:23:35,140
Well, let's head home.
Guess I'll get to work.

298
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:38,080
Hey, wait up!

299
00:23:38,080 --> 00:23:40,880
Then what happens to my debt?

300
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:46,100
Ryo-san, sorry,
but let's pretend this deal never happened.

301
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:47,480
No way.

302
00:23:50,080 --> 00:23:54,340
At least take 50% off, no,
even 20% off, or even 10% is fine...

303
00:23:54,340 --> 00:23:56,180
Just make it cheaper.

304
00:24:03,580 --> 00:24:08,720
The venue's booked and invitations have
gone out to all the relatives, oh no.

305
00:24:09,100 --> 00:24:14,080
What were you thinking, Dad? Maria's a man!
There's no way they can get married!

306
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:17,720
And you even went and arranged a samba
carnival parade with an open-top car!

307
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:21,900
Next time: Lightning wedding, Kankichi Ryotsu.
See you!

308
00:24:30,420 --> 00:24:37,160
People say I'm a woman
who can't fall in love,

309
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:42,960
but I've got a mountain
of things I want to do!

310
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

311
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,180
I want to be freer than a bird.

312
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:07,120
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

313
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:15,280
Heart of love, sorry, wait for me.

314
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:22,240
Panorama of the future, soon so dazzling.

315
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:26,535
You understand, right?

316
00:25:26,585 --> 00:25:30,080
Sorry, wait for me.

